{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/889853-lodge-of-arms","id":889853,"title":"Lodge of Arms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-13T07:05:56-07:00","id":889853,"title":"Lodge of Arms","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hi. Trying to recreate the Lodge of Arms for one of my games (also lodge of prophecy and lodge of voices). Here's what I have so far.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Siskur Dah benefit is a little lackluster, but I want it to be more interesting than a single bonus to weaponry or something. I mostly stole it from a 1e fetish (Lucky's Brother). The Forging Arms rite just confers the 1e benefit of the Lodge of Arms (+3 to rolls with one weapon, +1 to all others of it's type), which I thought was a bit too powerful to use as the Blessing or Siskur Dah benefit, but I could be wrong. The fluff would stay the <a href=\"http://nwod.org/wiki/index.php/Lodge_of_Arms\" target=\"_blank\">same</a> as in 1e. Same totem, etc.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing:</b> A Lodge member adds 5 dice rather than 3 when spending Willpower to augment an attack roll against another weapon user.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Aspiration: </b>To defeat a worthy opponent (Weaponry/Firearms user with equivalent dots in Skill)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ban: </b>A Lodge member can never refuse a challenge or duel issued by a weapon user.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sacred Hunt: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Disarm maneuvers automatically fail against an Uratha under the effects of the Lodge of Arms\u2019 Siskur Dah.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Further, the weapons of an Uratha under this effect always find their way back to their owner. If the owner loses track of weapon in battle (generally by throwing it at someone or sticking it into an enemy and letting go), a knife may slip out of the wound somehow. Others overlook the weapon, and so it remains to be reclaimed by its owner. The more time the Uratha has spent with a weapon, the more powerful this effect becomes. A dedicated, treasured, or long-held weapon finds some way to leave the battlefield with its owner, no matter what. Someone steps on it without noticing, flipping it into a backpack that the weapon\u2019s wielder later grabs as she leaves, or something even more improbable may happen.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lodge of Arms Rite: Bond of Steel (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is the central rite of the Lodge of Arms, a rite which bonds a spirit to a weapon and both to the lodge member who will carry the weapon for the rest of his life. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Performing the Rite:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rite only takes place after days of preparation. Once all the elements are in place \u2014 the weapon built, a spirit captured and bound and the werewolf\u2019s own spiritual aspect exhausted by days of endurance \u2014 the rite begins. Under the command of the Ritemaster, the new initiate carries out repeated sets of practiced forms with the weapon. They can be anything from a series of guards, parries and attacks with a blade to different \ufb01ring positions and target shots with a gun. As the new weapon-holder works, the lodge members who built the weapon and helped trap the spirits chant the words of the ritual with increasing volume and speed. The new initiate is expected to match these changes by increasing the speed and intensity of his exercises. This continues until the initiate is at the very point of exhaustion. Then, just before the young werewolf collapses, the ritemaster speaks the words of binding in the spirit tongue, and the spirits of the werewolf and blade momentarily fuse, infusing each other with new strength. Each of the participants in the rite, bar the initiate, spends a point of Essence to achieve this.This experience is often traumatic for both the initiate and the participants, causing them to lose control and frenzy. For that reason, all the participants in the rite must be experienced lodge members who can easily restrain the new lodge members without doing any serious permanent harm. Then the rite ends and the werewolf\u2019s new partnership begins.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b> Extended (20 successes; each roll represents 1 minute)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost</b>: 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll Results</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure: All successes are lost. The rite fails; if the subject also failed her Dexterity + Performance roll (see below), she cannot be inducted into the Lodge of Arms. If subject is already a member, she loses her membership in the Lodge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b> No successes are gained.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> Successes are gained toward the total. If the total successes equal 30 or more, the rite is completed. The subject is successfully initiated into the lodge, and gains the requisite </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">bond with her weapon. A lodge member gains a +3 modi\ufb01er to any attack roll using that weapon and that weapon only. Additionally, a lodge member may treat her Firearms or Weaponry Skill as being one level higher for all weapons of the same type.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> Successes are gained toward the total. If the total successes equal 35 or more, the rite is completed with an exceptional performance. All participants, including the subject, regain any spent points of Willpower from the invigorating experience.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Suggested Modi\ufb01ers</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rite\u2019s subject rolls Dexterity + Performance during the course of the rite to represent her own level of performance. Each success gained on this roll adds one die to the ritemaster\u2019s roll. If the roll is failed, the ritemaster instead loses two dice from her roll to perform the rite; if the subject dramatically fails this roll, the rite fails utterly and she is forbidden from joining the lodge. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 05-13-2016, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:18:28-07:00","id":889864,"title":"","content":"I see what you mean with the Siskur-Dah blessing. Maybe keep the disarm protection, but factor in some sort of benefit to resist abilities that would make them unable to use their weapon, like things that cause Arm Wrack or paralysis? That would probably get tricky, too.<br /> <br /> Adding a Renown to your Weapon roll seems a little easy. Maybe the weapon gains a bit of the blessing of the predator's jaw? Where it gains some extra Lethal depending on your form, and acts as a supernatural weapon that goes through normal abilities that downgrade Lethal? I like the idea of potentially going into gauru or even Kuruth and still not letting go of your sword.<br /> <br /> Also I think the Rite is a bit much. I get where you're going with it, and it's being honest to the original, but it's a fairly expensive rite you might only use once, and even then likely only on other werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-13-2016, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:33:37-07:00","id":889876,"title":"","content":"Adding Primal Urge to your Weapon's Damage Rating would be my go to for the basic effect, with the Predator's Jaw blessing as nofather suggested. Your weapon being a deadly weapon against your target of the Hunt seems to be the desired intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T09:56:51-07:00","id":889992,"title":"","content":"Maybe make it so that you can use a specific type of weapon even when when you're Raging perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}